# Managed by Ansible — openclaw.node.common role. Do not edit on the host;
# change the role and re-run a playbook that includes it.
#
# Reports the openclaw version ACTUALLY installed on this host, so drift is
# visible in Zabbix without waiting for — or trusting — a convergence run. The
# original sin this guards against is in openclaw-fleet-update.sh's header: a
# failed rollout erased its own evidence and the fleet sat un-upgraded for two
# months with nothing reporting it.
#
# Read from npm's package.json rather than by running `openclaw --version`:
# the CLI spawns a node process that can take seconds, and the agent's default
# Timeout is 3s — a slow UserParameter reports as unsupported, not as slow.
#
# The path is templated from openclaw_npm_prefix, not hardcoded: the gateway's
# global npm prefix is /usr/local while every other node's is /usr (see
# CLAUDE.md). A hardcoded /usr here would report nothing on the gateway forever.
#
# No `$` anywhere on the UserParameter line on purpose — the agent treats $1..$9
# in a UserParameter as positional arguments, so a shell variable there needs
# UnsafeUserParameters or escaping. Reading one known path avoids the question.
#
# The three k8s nodes are NOT covered by this file. They have no host-level
# agent (removed in a3c4e75 in favour of the in-cluster DaemonSet); that agent
# reads the very same package.json through its read-only /hostfs/root mount of
# the host filesystem, configured in homelab-gitops.
UserParameter={{ openclaw_zabbix_version_key }},sed -n 's/.*"version"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' {{ openclaw_npm_prefix.stdout | trim }}/lib/node_modules/openclaw/package.json | head -1
